# MoveBreak AI (repo: WorkAlarm)

School-project web app. Not medical software. Prefer a working demo over feature count.

## Communication

- Talk to the user in Thai.
- Plans, code, commit messages, and file comments stay in English.

## How to work

- Read `docs/` before implementing. Docs are guidelines, not a rigid spec. Keep a reasonable existing structure; do not refactor just to match the folder tree.
- Work one milestone at a time (~45 min) from `docs/05_45_MINUTE_TASK_PLAN.md`. Inspect the repo first. If a milestone is too large, split it.
- After each milestone: run/build, fix obvious errors, summarize changes, list files, give a short manual test. Stop unless asked to continue.
- No extra features, large unrelated refactors, or enterprise architecture. Prefer simple React hooks and modules.

## V1 stack (only)

React + Vite + TypeScript, Tailwind, MediaPipe Pose Landmarker (`@mediapipe/tasks-vision`), `getUserMedia()`, Canvas overlay, timestamp timer, Web Audio API, IndexedDB.

## Forbidden in V1

Backend, Firebase/Supabase, paid API, YOLO, OpenCV.js unless truly required, custom model training, uploading webcam frames.

## Timer

Source of truth: `targetTime = Date.now() + durationMs`. Remaining time is derived from `Date.now()`. Do not decrement a counter as truth.

## Pose

No inference queue — if inference is running, skip the frame. First exercise is **Both Arms Raised** (wrists above shoulders, landmarks visible, hold 3–5s). Do not complete on a single matching frame. Do not add more exercises until this one is reliable.

## Safety / demo

Include camera errors, no-person-detected, Emergency Skip, and a short demo timer (e.g. 10 seconds). Do not claim the app can force the user at OS level.
